Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Registers the `capivasign-icp://` deep link so the CapivaSign web page can
; launch the local signing agent. EDIT the path below to where CapivaSign.exe is
; installed, then double-click this file (per-user; no admin needed).
;
; Only needed for a manual/portable install — the installer (installer.iss)
; writes the per-machine equivalent for you.
;
; The web page triggers e.g.:
;   capivasign-icp://sign?baseUrl=https%3A%2F%2Fapp.capivapp.com.br&token=<RECIPIENT_TOKEN>&source=windows-my
; Windows passes the full URI as %1 to the agent, which prompts for cert/PIN,
; signs, and calls back into CapivaSign via /complete.
;
; NOTE: point this at CapivaSign.exe (the WINDOWED launcher), never at
; CapivaSignCli.exe. The CLI build is a console binary, so using it here makes a
; cmd window pop up on every signature request.
;
; SECURITY: also set ICP_ALLOWED_ORIGIN (system env) to your CapivaSign origin so
; the agent refuses to talk to any other host.

[HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Classes\capivasign-icp]
@="URL:CapivaSign ICP-Brasil Signing"
"URL Protocol"=""

[HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Classes\capivasign-icp\shell\open\command]
@="\"C:\\Program Files\\CapivaSign\\CapivaSign.exe\" \"%1\""
